  "discussion": {
    "headline": "Damp, Dreary, rainy and Much Cooler next week",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Friday, September 18, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "Thursday's heavy showers and torrential downpours ended up being more widespread than anticipated on Tuesday. None of the showers produced lightning or strong wind gusts, but they dumped 0.50-1.50\" of rain on the Route 11/Interstate 83 corridors of south-central PA. Outside of the eastern half of the Lower Susquehanna Valley, much less rain fell across northern MD, far southeastern PA and in Adams/Franklin Counties (see below). …",
